Recall browser extension

Provenance: vendored from https://github.com/tlsnotary/tlsn-extension at tag
0.1.0.1501 (commit 68bbd380d6e1a89d79748e5294661c752f5d1205), repository root
minus the parts listed below. The npm workspaces kept are packages/common,
packages/plugin-sdk and packages/extension, with upstream's package-lock.json
as the base. Recall's changes are listed below and in this repository's git
history.

Removed from upstream (not needed by Recall, or page-facing attack surface):
- Repository: app/ (mobile app), servers/ (Recall vendors the verifier
  separately in ../witness), .github/ and the other tooling dot-directories,
  the top-level docs (README.md, PLUGIN.md, RELEASING.md, VERIFIER.md and a
  contributor guide), .easignore, and the mobile root dependencies and scripts.
- Workspaces: packages/demo, packages/eas-webhook, packages/tlsn-mobile,
  packages/tlsn-wasm (wasm build script; the npm tlsn-wasm package is used),
  packages/ts-plugin-sample, packages/tutorial and packages/plugins (demo
  plugins).
- packages/extension, the page-facing plugin API: the content script and the
  window.tlsn / execCode page bridge (src/entries/Content), the plugin
  confirmation popup (src/entries/ConfirmPopup), the managed-window, overlay
  and request-interception code (src/background), the background EXEC_CODE,
  window, overlay, progress-routing and relay handlers, the offscreen plugin
  handlers (EXEC_CODE_OFFSCREEN, GET_PLUGIN_STATS_OFFSCREEN, RELAY_DELIVER*),
  SessionManager's page relay mode and its sessionData.proxyBase override,
  the manifest's content_scripts, web_accessible_resources and webRequest /
  windows permissions, helpers used only by those parts, and their tests.
- Browser (Playwright) test suites and their devDependencies in
  packages/extension and packages/plugin-sdk; STORE_LISTING.md,
  test-session-manager.html, a contributor guide and unused images.

Recall changes in packages/extension:
- manifest: name Recall, action popup, externally_connectable for the Recall
  web app origins, storage permission.
- src/entries/Popup and src/recall: the Recall popup, settings, witness health
  check, build flags and UI tokens.
- src/offscreen/ProveManager/index.ts: keeps the witness's signed
  `attestation` from session_completed; root_certs come from the build-time
  dev CA (RECALL_DEV_CA_DER_B64) when set.
- webpack.config.js: popup entry, @recall/evidence and @recall/net aliases,
  Recall build flags, a single React copy.
- src/entries/Background and src/entries/Offscreen: reduced to what the popup
  and the offscreen prover need.

